response:
 In one lap, Joneal covers 50 feet; in $\frac{5280}{50}=105\frac{3}{5}$ laps he will have run.  Hence the total distance traveled is equal to 5280 feet, the circumference of one lap.  Hence Joneal must have just completed a $360^{\text{o}}$ angle.  Therefore, he travels through each of $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ equally, which means he must have stopped at $\boxed{B}.$ [asy]
size(200); real x0=3/5; draw(Circle((0,0),1)); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10));
path [] zeroes(real r, real a, real b, real c, real d, real e, real f) {
  return ((0,0)--origin*a + r,0)--((0,d)--((0,f)--origin*(b-c) + d)--(0,f);
}
void quintile(real r, real a, real b, real c, real d, real e, real f) {
  zeroes(r,2^0*(a+1),a-b,a,b,2^0*(c+1),f);
  zeroes(r,2^0*(c+1),c-b,b,b,2^0*(d+1),f);
  zeroes(r,2^0*(d+1),d-b,d,d,2^0*(e+1),f);
  zeroes(r,1,1-1,0,e-1,0,f);
}
quintile(1,-1,-2,-3,3,- 4,2);
[/asy] </think> <answer> B </answer>

