&= \left(a - \frac{b + c}{2}\right)^2 + 3 = \frac{a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + bc - 2ab - 2ac + 3}{4}. \\
&= \frac{a^2 + (b - c)^2 - 2ac + bc - 2ab}{4} \\
&= \frac{a^2 + (b - c)^2 - (2b + 2c) a}{4}.
\end{align*}From here, we can make the substitution $x = b + c$ to get
\begin{align*}
&\frac{a^2 + (b - c)^2 - (2b + 2c) a}{4} \\
